{"id":"28c76f558d9d17b5","group":"58","path":"58/batch03/58-ax-equality-predicate-substitution.md","title":"Equality Predicate Substitution Axiom","display":"ax-equality-predicate-substitution — Equality Predicate Substitution Axiom","type":"axiom","metadata":{"type":"axiom","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-ax-equality-predicate-substitution","aliases":["58-ax-equality-predicate-substitution"],"display":"ax-equality-predicate-substitution — Equality Predicate Substitution Axiom","depends_on":["[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]","[[../batch06/58-df-atomic-formula.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"axiom"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-ax-equality-predicate-substitution"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-ax-equality-predicate-substitution</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"ax-equality-predicate-substitution — Equality Predicate Substitution Axiom"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"ca5c1762b574813b\" href=\"?note=ca5c1762b574813b\" title=\"../batch06/58-df-atomic-formula.md\">../batch06/58-df-atomic-formula.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\\in V\">\\(\\Sigma\\in V\\)</span>, with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RelSym},\\mathrm{RelAr},\\mathrm{Fml}_S,\\mathrm{Trm}_S:V\\to V\">\\(\\mathrm{RelSym},\\mathrm{RelAr},\\mathrm{Fml}_S,\\mathrm{Trm}_S:V\\to V\\)</span> (the relation-symbol and arity projections of the signature contract in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}(\\mathrm{RelAr}(\\Sigma),\\mathrm{RelSym}(\\Sigma),\\omega)\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}(\\mathrm{RelAr}(\\Sigma),\\mathrm{RelSym}(\\Sigma),\\omega)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega\\land R\\in\\mathrm{RelSym}(\\Sigma)\\land\\mathrm{RelAr}(\\Sigma)(R)=n\">\\(n\\in\\omega\\land R\\in\\mathrm{RelSym}(\\Sigma)\\land\\mathrm{RelAr}(\\Sigma)(R)=n\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"ca5c1762b574813b\" href=\"?note=ca5c1762b574813b\" title=\"../batch06/58-df-atomic-formula.md\">../batch06/58-df-atomic-formula.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\bar s,\\bar t\\in\\mathrm{Trm}_S(\\Sigma)^n\">\\(\\bar s,\\bar t\\in\\mathrm{Trm}_S(\\Sigma)^n\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{EqPredicateSubstitution}_S(\\Sigma)\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\">\\(\\mathrm{EqPredicateSubstitution}_S(\\Sigma)\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\)</span> (axiom-schema instance set defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}equality\\text{-}predicate\\text{-}substitution\\text{-}schema} \\vdash \\mathrm{EqPredicateSubstitution}_S(\\Sigma)\\coloneqq\\left\\{\\left(\\bigwedge_{i&lt;n}s_i\\doteq t_i\\right)\\to\\left(R(\\bar s)\\leftrightarrow R(\\bar t)\\right):n\\in\\omega\\land R\\in\\mathrm{RelSym}(\\Sigma)\\land\\mathrm{RelAr}(\\Sigma)(R)=n\\land\\bar s,\\bar t\\in\\mathrm{Trm}_S(\\Sigma)^n\\right\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}equality\\text{-}predicate\\text{-}substitution\\text{-}schema} \\vdash \\mathrm{EqPredicateSubstitution}_S(\\Sigma)\\coloneqq\\left\\{\\left(\\bigwedge_{i&lt;n}s_i\\doteq t_i\\right)\\to\\left(R(\\bar s)\\leftrightarrow R(\\bar t)\\right):n\\in\\omega\\land R\\in\\mathrm{RelSym}(\\Sigma)\\land\\mathrm{RelAr}(\\Sigma)(R)=n\\land\\bar s,\\bar t\\in\\mathrm{Trm}_S(\\Sigma)^n\\right\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R(\\bar s)\">\\(R(\\bar s)\\)</span> abbreviates the atomic formula <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R(s_0,\\ldots,s_{n-1})\">\\(R(s_0,\\ldots,s_{n-1})\\)</span>; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\doteq\">\\(\\doteq\\)</span> is the object-language equality symbol, not equality of term codes.</li>\n<li>For <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n=0\">\\(n=0\\)</span>, the empty conjunction is <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\top\">\\(\\top\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Equality is congruent for every relation symbol of the signature.</li>\n<li>The relation-symbol set and its arity map are obtained by explicit projections from <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span>, rather than by an untyped English-only component description.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch17/58-df-formula.md","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-formul